{
  "dom_id": "step-q121692",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/6160de33d6b9e0cbd5cdfea19979a682398996f164e9654864ca8530d2048b51.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram above represents a universal set $S,$ two sets $A$ and $B,$ and the number of elements in each region of $S.$ An element from $A$ is selected at random. Calculate $P({B}^{′}|A).$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute $P({B}^{′}|A),$ we need to ask, \"what is the probability of $B$ *not* occurring given that $A$ has occurred?\"\n\nSince we are assuming that $A$ has occurred, we only consider the elements inside $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/cc16bfcd6588617a9181cb3798fbaba33a6cff3f1fb05b47d311d14bea3fb9f5.png)\n\nIn total, the number of elements inside $A$ is\n\n$$\n8+2=10.\n$$\n\nOf these $10$ elements, $8$ lie outside of $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/4519280f1825097c175d9dd5636b3fb1cb59c5849b93fa07a6416056fa51b42f.png)\n\nSince each outcome is equally likely, $P({B}^{′}|A)$ can be interpreted as the proportion of ${B}^{′}$ that lies inside $A,$ relative to the size of $A.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}|A) & =\\frac{8}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
